VDR Plugin 'mcp' Revision History
---------------------------------

2026-11-08: Version 0.4.3

- Fix the Makefile: -fPIC was missing in CFLAGS and CXXFLAGS, the plugin did
  not link when VDR's pkg-config file does not provide it.

2026-11-05: Version 0.4.2

- VDR does not shut down while vdr_genindex runs (cPlugin::Active()).
- The deny list can no longer lose entries unnoticed: a stray argument
  (blank in a list) or --deny without '=' stops the plugin with an error,
  and the log shows the list in effect at every start.
- README rewritten: quick start, examples, security, troubleshooting,
  Debian packaging.

2026-11-05: Version 0.4.1

- KEYADD also shows how to use the new key: the ready command line for
  Claude Code, URL and header for other clients, the certificate to trust.

2026-11-04: Version 0.4.0

- MCP over HTTPS ("Streamable HTTP", --http=ADDR:PORT, off by default) for
  clients without SSH, with API keys (ro/rw) managed over SVDRP
  (PLUG mcp KEYADD/KEYLIST/KEYDEL) and a self-signed certificate created at
  the first start. Read only keys see only listing tools (--ro-allow).
- MCP clients cannot call the plugin's own SVDRP commands via vdr_PLUG.

2026-11-04: Version 0.3.0

- New tools vdr_marks, vdr_setmarks and vdr_genindex: read and replace the
  editing marks of a recording, regenerate its index in the background and
  thereby count its errors. SVDRP offers neither.

2026-11-04: Version 0.2.1

- vdr_log skips the plugin's own log lines of vdr_log calls, which contain
  the filter text and therefore matched every filter.

2026-11-04: Version 0.2.0

- New tool vdr_log (option --log[=UNIT], off by default): the newest lines of
  the systemd journal of VDR, optionally filtered by a text. Needs the user
  vdr in the group systemd-journal.

2026-11-04: Version 0.1.2

- mcp.conf sets --deny=DEL*,HITK, so the file shows what is denied. The
  same list stays the default if the option is missing.

2026-11-04: Version 0.1.1

- HITK (remote control keys) is denied by default, the default deny list is
  now DEL*,HITK.

2026-11-04: Version 0.1.0

- Initial revision: MCP server on 127.0.0.1:6420 (MCP stdio format over TCP,
  one JSON-RPC message per line) that offers every SVDRP command of VDR and
  of the loaded plugins as a tool, built at runtime from SVDRP HELP.
- Deny list for commands (--deny, default DEL*).
